.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt MESG 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mesg
.Nd control terminal write permission
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op y | n
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reports whether other users may write to the current terminal.
With
.Ql y
it attempts to allow writes and with
.Ql n
to refuse them by changing the terminal's group-write bit.
.Pp
The current
.Pa tty:console
server exposes a fixed mode and has no chmod operation, so the query works
but a set request fails. That is the exact
.Ql P4u-D1
follow-up.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
The query exits 0 when writes are allowed and 1 when they are refused.
A failed set or usage error exits non-zero.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tty 1 ,
.Xr stty 1
.Sh STANDARDS
IEEE Std 1003.1-2024
.Pq POSIX.1-2024 ,
except the unavailable set path noted above.
